{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f1e2d3c4-b5a6-7890-1234-567890abcdef",
    "name": "Feathr Distributed Event Processing Platform",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Distributed Event Processing Platform.\n\n## Quick start\n\n1. Make sure the stack is running:\n   ```\n   cd feathr-events && docker compose up -d\n   ```\n2. Confirm health: send `Health / GET /health` — should return `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`.\n3. Optionally seed events via the `Ingestion / POST /events (happy path)` request.\n4. Explore the four query endpoints under `Queries`.\n\n## Variables\n\n- `baseUrl` — defaults to `http://localhost:8000`. Override for staging / production.\n- `userId` — used as the example user for filter requests.\n- `eventType` — used as the example event type for filter requests.\n- `lastEventId` — auto-set by the `POST /events` test script so follow-up requests can reference it.\n- `windowStart`, `windowEnd` — used by stats / search date-range requests.\n\n## Structure\n\nFolders mirror the API surface:\n\n- **Health** — liveness + queue observability.\n- **Ingestion** — `POST /events` happy path + every validation error case.\n- **Queries** — list / stats / search / realtime, including filter combinations and 422 cases.\n- **Workflow examples** — sequenced requests showing the full ingest → query lifecycle.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Liveness and observability endpoints. The rate limiter is exempt from `/health*`, so these stay available even under abuse.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health (liveness)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status: ok', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.deep.equal({status: 'ok'});",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Always returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` once the app process is up. Used by container healthchecks and external uptime monitors. Exempt from the rate limiter."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /health/queue (observability snapshot)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('exposes worker counters', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  ['queue_depth','queue_in_flight','dlq_depth','processed','failed','dead_lettered','duplicates_suppressed']",
                  "    .forEach(k => pm.expect(body).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/queue",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health", "queue"]
            },
            "description": "Snapshot of queue + worker counters: queue depth, in-flight messages, DLQ depth, processed / failed / dead-lettered totals, and duplicate-suppression count. Used by ops dashboards and the integration test suite."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ingestion",
      "description": "`POST /events` — validates the payload and enqueues it for async processing. Returns `202 Accepted` with the server-generated `event_id`. Persistence to MongoDB and indexing in Elasticsearch happen in the background worker.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /events (happy path)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns status + event_id', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('accepted');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.event_id).to.be.a('string').and.have.length(32);",
                  "});",
                  "// Capture event_id for downstream requests in the workflow folder.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lastEventId', body.event_id);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"click\",\n  \"user_id\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://feathr.co/spring-campaign\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"campaign\": \"spring-2026\",\n    \"label\": \"hero-cta\",\n    \"browser\": \"chrome\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "Submit a single event. `timestamp` is optional — if omitted, the server stamps `now()`. `metadata` is a free-form JSON object capped at 64 top-level keys.\n\nResponse shape:\n```json\n{\"status\": \"accepted\", \"event_id\": \"a1b2c3...\"}\n```"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /events (with explicit timestamp)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"conversion\",\n  \"user_id\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://feathr.co/checkout\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-25T16:00:00Z\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"campaign\": \"spring-2026\",\n    \"amount\": 99.99\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "Producer-provided timestamp. Useful for backfill or events buffered client-side."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /events (event_type normalized to lowercase)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"PageView\",\n  \"user_id\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://feathr.co/\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "`event_type` is normalized to lowercase server-side so reporting doesn't fragment across capitalization variants (`PageView`, `pageview`, `PAGEVIEW`)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /events (validation: missing user_id) [422]",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422 Unprocessable Entity', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('mentions missing field', () => {",
                  "  const detail = JSON.stringify(pm.response.json().detail);",
                  "  pm.expect(detail).to.include('user_id');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"click\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://feathr.co\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "Required-field validation. `user_id` (and `event_type`, `source_url`) are mandatory."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /events (validation: invalid URL) [422]",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422 Unprocessable Entity', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"click\",\n  \"user_id\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"source_url\": \"not a valid url\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "URL validation. `source_url` must parse as a valid HTTP(S) URL."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /events (validation: extra field forbidden) [422]",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422 Unprocessable Entity', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('rejects extra fields', () => {",
                  "  const detail = JSON.stringify(pm.response.json().detail);",
                  "  pm.expect(detail).to.include('extra_forbidden');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"click\",\n  \"user_id\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://feathr.co\",\n  \"unexpected_field\": \"value\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "Strict schema. Extra top-level fields are rejected to keep producers honest about the contract."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /events (validation: empty event_type) [422]",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"\",\n  \"user_id\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://feathr.co\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "Empty strings on required string fields are rejected."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /events (validation: oversized metadata) [422]",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"click\",\n  \"user_id\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://feathr.co\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"k1\":1,\"k2\":2,\"k3\":3,\"k4\":4,\"k5\":5,\"k6\":6,\"k7\":7,\"k8\":8,\"k9\":9,\"k10\":10,\n    \"k11\":1,\"k12\":2,\"k13\":3,\"k14\":4,\"k15\":5,\"k16\":6,\"k17\":7,\"k18\":8,\"k19\":9,\"k20\":10,\n    \"k21\":1,\"k22\":2,\"k23\":3,\"k24\":4,\"k25\":5,\"k26\":6,\"k27\":7,\"k28\":8,\"k29\":9,\"k30\":10,\n    \"k31\":1,\"k32\":2,\"k33\":3,\"k34\":4,\"k35\":5,\"k36\":6,\"k37\":7,\"k38\":8,\"k39\":9,\"k40\":10,\n    \"k41\":1,\"k42\":2,\"k43\":3,\"k44\":4,\"k45\":5,\"k46\":6,\"k47\":7,\"k48\":8,\"k49\":9,\"k50\":10,\n    \"k51\":1,\"k52\":2,\"k53\":3,\"k54\":4,\"k55\":5,\"k56\":6,\"k57\":7,\"k58\":8,\"k59\":9,\"k60\":10,\n    \"k61\":1,\"k62\":2,\"k63\":3,\"k64\":4,\"k65\":5\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"]
            },
            "description": "Metadata is capped at 64 top-level keys (defense in depth against partner-side bugs that would otherwise blow out the Elasticsearch field mapping)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Queries",
      "description": "Read-only query endpoints. Mongo backs `/events` and `/events/stats`; Elasticsearch backs `/events/search`; Redis caches `/events/stats/realtime`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /events (no filter)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns items array + paging metadata', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('items');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('count');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('skip');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('limit');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events?limit=20&sort=desc",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "limit", "value": "20"},
                {"key": "sort", "value": "desc"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "List the most recent events. `sort=desc` is the default; results are paged via `skip`/`limit`. Maximum `limit` is 1000."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events (filter by event_type)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events?event_type={{eventType}}&limit=100",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "event_type", "value": "{{eventType}}"},
                {"key": "limit", "value": "100"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Filter by event type. Backed by the `(event_type, timestamp desc)` Mongo index for fast lookups."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events (filter by user_id)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events?user_id={{userId}}&limit=100",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "user_id", "value": "{{userId}}"},
                {"key": "limit", "value": "100"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Per-user history. Backed by the `(user_id, timestamp desc)` Mongo index."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events (filter by source_url)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events?source_url=https://feathr.co/spring-campaign&limit=100",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "source_url", "value": "https://feathr.co/spring-campaign"},
                {"key": "limit", "value": "100"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exact-URL filter. Not directly indexed in Mongo (see ARCHITECTURE.md §5 — indexes deliberately not added) but performant because the `event_type, timestamp` index narrows the working set first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events (filter by date range)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events?start={{windowStart}}&end={{windowEnd}}&limit=100",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "start", "value": "{{windowStart}}"},
                {"key": "end", "value": "{{windowEnd}}"},
                {"key": "limit", "value": "100"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Half-open window: `start <= timestamp < end`. Composes cleanly when chaining requests."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events (combined filters)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events?user_id={{userId}}&event_type={{eventType}}&start={{windowStart}}&end={{windowEnd}}&limit=100",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "user_id", "value": "{{userId}}"},
                {"key": "event_type", "value": "{{eventType}}"},
                {"key": "start", "value": "{{windowStart}}"},
                {"key": "end", "value": "{{windowEnd}}"},
                {"key": "limit", "value": "100"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "All filters are AND-combined."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events (pagination via skip + limit)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events?limit=2&skip=2",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "limit", "value": "2"},
                {"key": "skip", "value": "2"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Skip-based pagination. `limit` is capped at 1000; `skip` is capped at 100,000."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/stats (day bucket)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns bucketed counts', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.bucket).to.eql('day');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('items');",
                  "  if (body.items.length > 0) {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.items[0]).to.have.all.keys('event_type','bucket_start','count');",
                  "  }",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/stats?start={{windowStart}}&end={{windowEnd}}&bucket=day",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "stats"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "start", "value": "{{windowStart}}"},
                {"key": "end", "value": "{{windowEnd}}"},
                {"key": "bucket", "value": "day"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Mongo aggregation pipeline grouping events by type and time bucket. Returns one row per `(event_type, bucket_start)`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/stats (hour bucket)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/stats?start={{windowStart}}&end={{windowEnd}}&bucket=hour",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "stats"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "start", "value": "{{windowStart}}"},
                {"key": "end", "value": "{{windowEnd}}"},
                {"key": "bucket", "value": "hour"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Hourly buckets. Use for narrow windows (e.g., last 24h)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/stats (week bucket, ISO Monday)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/stats?start={{windowStart}}&end={{windowEnd}}&bucket=week",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "stats"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "start", "value": "{{windowStart}}"},
                {"key": "end", "value": "{{windowEnd}}"},
                {"key": "bucket", "value": "week"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Weekly buckets aligned to Monday (ISO 8601). Mongo's `$dateTrunc` default is Sunday; we pin Monday explicitly."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/stats (validation: missing window) [422]",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/stats",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "stats"]
            },
            "description": "Both `start` and `end` are required."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/stats (validation: invalid bucket) [422]",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/stats?start={{windowStart}}&end={{windowEnd}}&bucket=month",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "stats"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "start", "value": "{{windowStart}}"},
                {"key": "end", "value": "{{windowEnd}}"},
                {"key": "bucket", "value": "month"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "`bucket` must be one of `hour`, `day`, `week`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/search (full-text via Elasticsearch)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns items + count', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('items');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('count');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/search?q=spring",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "search"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "q", "value": "spring"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Full-text search over `metadata.*` and `source_url.text`. The `simple_query_string` query uses `lenient: true` so numeric metadata fields don't break unrelated text searches."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/search (with event_type filter)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/search?q=spring&event_type=click",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "search"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "q", "value": "spring"},
                {"key": "event_type", "value": "click"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Combine free-text search with structured filters."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/search (with date range)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/search?q=campaign&start={{windowStart}}&end={{windowEnd}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "search"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "q", "value": "campaign"},
                {"key": "start", "value": "{{windowStart}}"},
                {"key": "end", "value": "{{windowEnd}}"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Free-text + date filter."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/search (URL path fragment)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/search?q=checkout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "search"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "q", "value": "checkout"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "URLs are indexed both as `keyword` (exact match) and via a `text` subfield (path-fragment match). Searching for `checkout` finds `https://feathr.co/checkout`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/search (validation: missing q) [422]",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/search",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "search"]
            },
            "description": "`q` is required."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/stats/realtime (Redis-cached summary)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns realtime summary shape', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('cache_hit');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('window_seconds');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('total');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('by_type');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('generated_at');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('generated_at uses Z suffix (UTC)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().generated_at).to.match(/Z$/);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/stats/realtime",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "stats", "realtime"]
            },
            "description": "Lightweight rolling-window stats served from Redis with a configurable TTL (default 10s).\n\nFirst request is a cache miss (`cache_hit: false`); subsequent requests within the TTL window return the same cached payload (`cache_hit: true`). Single-flighted server-side to prevent dogpile under TTL expiry."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /events/stats/realtime (custom window)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/stats/realtime?window_seconds=600",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["events", "stats", "realtime"],
              "query": [
                {"key": "window_seconds", "value": "600"}
              ]
            },
            "description": "Custom rolling window (10 minutes here). Each `window_seconds` value gets its own cache key — concurrent requests for different windows do not invalidate each other."
          }
        }
      ]
